Gigliola Cinquetti "Non Ho L'Età"]

8
00:04:24,055 --> 00:04:26,057
continues playing]

9
00:05:34,668 --> 00:05:36,461
-[Youjin gasps]

10
00:05:36,545 --> 00:05:38,505
I'VE BEEN
DYING TO SEE YOU!

11
00:05:38,588 --> 00:05:40,590
WELCOME

12
00:05:49,099 --> 00:05:51,101
You didn't have to come all this way.

13
00:05:51,184 --> 00:05:53,311
You're the guest of honor.
Of course, I should.

14
00:05:53,395 --> 00:05:54,396
Let me take that.

15
00:05:54,479 --> 00:05:56,773
Leave it. I can get it.

16
00:05:56,857 --> 00:05:58,692
-I should take it.
-It's okay.

17
00:05:59,776 --> 00:06:02,195
I could've taken a cab.
Why did you come all this way?

18
00:06:02,279 --> 00:06:03,822
Got nothing better to do?

19
00:06:03,905 --> 00:06:06,032
[sighs] I've got plenty to do,
but I came anyway.

20
00:06:06,116 --> 00:06:08,285
Because I missed you so much.

21
00:06:09,119 --> 00:06:10,787
Well, I didn't get you any gifts.

22
00:06:11,872 --> 00:06:12,873
Okay.

23
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:15,208
Let's get a taxi.

24
00:06:15,292 --> 00:06:17,127
[exclaims softly] But I drove here.

25
00:06:19,254 --> 00:06:20,255
Did you buy a car?

26
00:06:21,423 --> 00:06:22,424
No.

27
00:06:23,216 --> 00:06:24,217
Huh?

28
00:06:34,936 --> 00:06:35,937
[Youjin] Hop in.

29
00:06:39,441 --> 00:06:41,443
Hey, why would you bring this out here?

30
00:06:42,527 --> 00:06:45,280
[Youjin] You have a lot of luggage,
and I figured you'd be tired.

31
00:06:45,363 --> 00:06:46,615
And taxis are expensive.

32
00:06:48,533 --> 00:06:50,994
My car is more expensive
than a taxi. Move.

33
00:06:52,787 --> 00:06:53,955
[Youjin] I'm a good driver.

34
00:06:54,039 --> 00:06:55,874
-I can get you home nice and comfortable.
-[Jihoon grunts]

35
00:06:56,458 --> 00:06:59,711
Hey, all I asked you to do
was water the plants

36
00:06:59,794 --> 00:07:01,129
and look after my place.

37
00:07:02,631 --> 00:07:04,758
You've been driving my car around,
haven't you?

38
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:05,842
No.

39
00:07:06,593 --> 00:07:09,888
-What do you take me for?
-[Jihoon grunting]

40
00:07:12,349 --> 00:07:13,391
-Give me that.
-Huh?

41
00:07:14,225 --> 00:07:15,435
I can drive.

42
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:18,563
[Jihoon] Just get in.

43
00:07:33,745 --> 00:07:36,289
-[Youjin] Huh?
-[Jihoon exclaims softly, scoffs]

44
00:07:41,878 --> 00:07:43,004
Put your seatbelt on.

45
00:07:43,088 --> 00:07:44,089
[Youjin] Okay.

46
00:07:45,006 --> 00:07:46,424
You've had a long flight,

47
00:07:47,342 --> 00:07:49,094
and you must be jet-lagged.

48
00:07:49,177 --> 00:07:50,512
Seriously, I can drive.

49
00:07:50,595 --> 00:07:51,846
Speak for yourself.

50
00:07:51,930 --> 00:07:55,767
You must be exhausted
from coursework, exams, and your thesis.

51
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:58,353
[inhales] So why'd you come
all the way out here?

52
00:07:58,436 --> 00:07:59,521
In my car, no less?

53
00:08:02,649 --> 00:08:03,650
Huh?

54
00:08:05,819 --> 00:08:08,530
Well... You know, Professor,

55
00:08:08,613 --> 00:08:11,032
you've got a lot of connections, right?

56
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,368
[Jihoon] I do. And?

57
00:08:14,369 --> 00:08:18,581
Do you know a Russian mathematician,
Aleksandr Lyapunov?

58
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:20,834
I hear he's super famous.

59
00:08:20,917 --> 00:08:22,210
I do.

60
00:08:22,293 --> 00:08:25,380
We're close. He died in 1918.

61
00:08:25,463 --> 00:08:27,132
[gasps] Yeah, him.

62
00:08:27,215 --> 00:08:28,216
-[Jihoon] Yeah?
-Yeah.

63
00:08:28,717 --> 00:08:30,510
I knew you'd know him.

64
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:42,355
KIM JISEOK AND LEE JIHYE
JANUARY 27, 2027, 2:00 PM

65
00:08:42,439 --> 00:08:43,440
PLEASE JOIN US

66
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:45,859
AT LAST, WE'VE FOUND THE ONE
TO SHARE OUR LIVES WITH

67
00:08:47,402 --> 00:08:49,404
FOR YOUR KIND WISHES
BRIDE LEE JIHYE

68
00:08:51,740 --> 00:08:52,824
ACCOUNT NUMBER COPIED

69
00:08:56,745 --> 00:08:58,413
CHECKING ACCOUNT
42,700 WON

70
00:08:59,831 --> 00:09:02,959
-[cellphone thuds]

71
00:09:10,175 --> 00:09:13,178
All solutions of the dynamical system

72
00:09:13,261 --> 00:09:18,016
that start near a Lyapunov-stable
equilibrium point stay near it forever.

73
00:09:21,144 --> 00:09:22,270
Forever.

74
00:09:26,316 --> 00:09:29,486
The above definition
can be understood as follows.

75
00:09:29,569 --> 00:09:33,823
Solutions that start sufficiently close
to a Lyapunov-stable equilibrium

76
00:09:33,907 --> 00:09:37,327
remain sufficiently close
to the equilibrium forever,

77
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:41,122
with the allowable deviation
being arbitrarily small.

78
00:09:43,792 --> 00:09:47,545
Solutions that start sufficiently close
to an asymptotically stable equilibrium

79
00:09:47,629 --> 00:09:49,631
not only stay close to it,

80
00:09:49,714 --> 00:09:52,801
but also eventually converge
to the equilibrium.

81
00:09:56,471 --> 00:10:00,350
Solutions that start sufficiently close
to an exponentially stable equilibrium

82
00:10:00,433 --> 00:10:03,978
eventually converge exponentially,

83
00:10:04,062 --> 00:10:07,440
at least as fast
as a particular known rate.

84
00:10:12,028 --> 00:10:13,780
Come to think of it, I'm kind of hurt.

85
00:10:15,156 --> 00:10:19,035
You went all the way to the States
and seriously didn't get me anything?

86
00:10:23,248 --> 00:10:26,376
It's Christmas soon.
You could've picked up a little something.

87
00:10:28,378 --> 00:10:30,380
Not even some chocolate or something?

88
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:32,048
Do you think I went there for fun?

89
00:10:32,132 --> 00:10:34,759
I was attending a conference.
I didn't have time for that.

90
00:10:35,802 --> 00:10:38,847
I mean, they sell chocolate
at the airport duty-free stores.

91
00:10:40,515 --> 00:10:42,976
It's not like
I want to eat American chocolate.

92
00:10:43,685 --> 00:10:46,187
It's the thought that counts, you know?

93
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:54,737
[exclaims] What's that?

94
00:10:55,238 --> 00:10:56,823
Are you giving me money instead?

95
00:10:58,366 --> 00:10:59,492
[Jihoon] Here. Your gift.

96
00:11:02,245 --> 00:11:03,246
What's this?

97
00:11:15,175 --> 00:11:16,926
I met Park Minjae there.

98
00:11:19,929 --> 00:11:22,265
I thought he was in Canada,
but he's in the US.

99
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:26,728
I asked him if he'd been in Canada,
and he said no.

100
00:11:27,353 --> 00:11:28,980
He said he went back to the States.

101
00:11:30,732 --> 00:11:32,901
Turns out he's working
on some project with MIT.

102
00:11:34,110 --> 00:11:35,111
Did you know?

103
00:11:37,739 --> 00:11:40,325
Other than his hairstyle,
he looked pretty much the same.

104
00:11:40,909 --> 00:11:42,577
He seemed to be doing well.

105
00:11:45,997 --> 00:11:47,457
I said you were doing well, too.

106
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:50,293
That you're eating well, attending school,
and studying hard.

107
00:11:52,629 --> 00:11:55,048
That's his new number,
so give him a call if you want.

108
00:11:59,928 --> 00:12:01,429
What would I even say?

109
00:12:02,639 --> 00:12:04,140
There's nothing to talk about.

110
00:12:07,018 --> 00:12:09,562
It's not like I'm going to cry
and curse him out.

111
00:12:12,941 --> 00:12:16,986
Well, breakups are hard
and painful for everyone.

112
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:19,697
Your relationship wasn't anything special.

113
00:12:19,781 --> 00:12:23,034
That's what relationships are like.
They can end just like that.

114
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,414
You know what, Professor?

115
00:12:29,415 --> 00:12:31,292
You talk too much.

116
00:12:31,376 --> 00:12:33,002
Because I know a lot.

117
00:12:33,836 --> 00:12:35,296
There's nothing I don't know.

118
00:12:38,299 --> 00:12:41,719
Have you never liked a woman before?

119
00:12:41,803 --> 00:12:42,804
Well...

120
00:12:44,097 --> 00:12:47,058
I've just never been dumped
by a woman I liked.

121
00:12:50,228 --> 00:12:52,313
I guess you never get hurt or anything.

122
00:12:52,397 --> 00:12:55,149
No. I'm a deep, grounded person.

123
00:12:59,862 --> 00:13:00,947
What?

124
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,121
Hey.

125
00:13:10,999 --> 00:13:13,835
Hey, no littering.
You should put it in a trash can.

126
00:13:15,461 --> 00:13:17,755
I pray that the woman he likes
brutally dumps him

127
00:13:17,839 --> 00:13:19,674
and leaves him in tears.

128
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:24,679
You're praying that happens
to Park Minjae, not me, right?

129
00:13:26,306 --> 00:13:28,474
No. To both of you.

130
00:15:17,375 --> 00:15:20,128
Oh... Youjin is home, so lock the doors.

131
00:15:23,256 --> 00:15:25,174
[Yongseok] Be gentle. I'm scared.

132
00:15:25,258 --> 00:15:28,052
Okay, stay still. I'm scared too. [gasps]

133
00:15:31,389 --> 00:15:32,390
What's up?

134
00:15:34,016 --> 00:15:35,434
[Youseong] Can I have 100,000 won?

135
00:15:35,518 --> 00:15:36,769
I don't have it.

136
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:39,105
You're not even going to ask why?

137
00:15:40,022 --> 00:15:42,358
You always say no
even without asking. Always.

138
00:15:44,527 --> 00:15:45,820
What do you need it for?

139
00:15:46,696 --> 00:15:47,947
[Youseong] I can't tell you.

140
00:15:48,865 --> 00:15:50,032
[mouthing] Jeez.

141
00:15:50,867 --> 00:15:53,327
[Youseong] Come on,
can't you just give me 100,000 won?

142
00:15:53,411 --> 00:15:55,788
There's a reason I need it.

143
00:15:56,873 --> 00:15:58,833
-Mom, just give me my allowance early.
-Hey!

144
00:15:58,916 --> 00:16:01,377
Jeez. You're not getting it early.

145
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,004
-[Youseong] Dad.
-Hey!

146
00:16:03,546 --> 00:16:06,549
Dude, the boss says no.

147
00:16:07,133 --> 00:16:08,134
Then what about me?

148
00:16:08,759 --> 00:16:10,428
What am I? Huh?

149
00:16:11,053 --> 00:16:13,973
I'm the eldest son
and the heir to the auto repair shop.

150
00:16:14,056 --> 00:16:15,766
I'll inherit the whole thing someday.

151
00:16:15,850 --> 00:16:17,935
You can't even do that much
for your own heir?

152
00:16:18,019 --> 00:16:19,812
Heir, my foot.

153
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:23,399
Honey, what do you think he's saying?

154
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:26,444
I don't know. I can't hear well right now.

155
00:16:27,570 --> 00:16:28,571
[Youseong] Then, Mom...

156
00:16:28,654 --> 00:16:29,655
[Miyoung, softly] Yeah.

157
00:16:29,739 --> 00:16:31,115
[Youseong] If you give me 100,000 won,

158
00:16:31,782 --> 00:16:33,534
I'll give you this.

159
00:16:34,202 --> 00:16:35,203
What is it?

160
00:16:35,995 --> 00:16:36,996
[Youseong] I don't know.

161
00:16:38,748 --> 00:16:39,999
You're drunk, aren't you?

162
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:43,753
Give me a break. Jeez.

163
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:14,867
NO RESULTS FOUND
MATCHING +1 (617) 555-0754

164
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:19,789
+1 (617) SERVES BOSTON, MASSACHUSETTS...

165
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:21,958
[Youseong] Massachusetts in the US?

166
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:23,584
[slurring] Messasuses?

167
00:17:25,962 --> 00:17:28,881
[groans] This is why I hate English.

168
00:17:29,882 --> 00:17:31,467
The pronunciation is just too hard.

169
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:54,365
-[line ringing]
-[sighs softly]

170
00:18:11,841 --> 00:18:14,760
Not answering. Not answering.

171
00:18:16,095 --> 00:18:17,680
-[sighs]
-[man in English]<i> Hello?</i>

172
00:18:18,973 --> 00:18:19,974
[in Korean] Hello?

173
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:21,851
[in Korean]<i> Yes, hello?</i>

174
00:18:23,227 --> 00:18:24,228
Uh...

175
00:18:24,312 --> 00:18:26,522
Are you in Massachusetts, by any chance?

176
00:18:26,606 --> 00:18:27,607
[man] <i>Pardon?</i>

177
00:18:28,274 --> 00:18:29,275
<i>Who are you?</i>

178
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:32,945
I said, are you in Massachusetts?

179
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:38,409
You're in the United...
I mean, America, right?

180
00:18:38,492 --> 00:18:39,910
[man] <i>Yes, I am. Who are you?</i>

181
00:18:39,994 --> 00:18:40,995
[in English] Hello?

182
00:18:41,996 --> 00:18:43,914
[man in English]<i> Hello? Hello?</i>

183
00:18:45,166 --> 00:18:46,167
[in English] Hello?

184
00:18:47,376 --> 00:18:48,377
[man in Korean]<i> What?</i>

185
00:18:49,337 --> 00:18:52,131
<i>I think you may have the wrong number.</i>

186
00:18:52,214 --> 00:18:54,008
<i>Who were you trying to call?</i>

187
00:18:54,091 --> 00:18:55,092
[in Korean] What?

188
00:18:56,010 --> 00:18:58,679
I'm Lim Youseong.

189
00:18:59,305 --> 00:19:00,431
I'm Korean.

190
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:03,934
Who are you?

191
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:17,466
A ghost?

192
00:20:31,105 --> 00:20:32,106
Ah...

193
00:23:23,652 --> 00:23:25,654
-[jewelry box snaps shut]

194
00:23:41,754 --> 00:23:44,214
[exclaims] It's bean sprout soup.

195
00:23:44,298 --> 00:23:47,509
It's all for our heir, our eldest son.

196
00:23:47,593 --> 00:23:49,762
We can't have him suffering
from a hangover.

197
00:23:52,264 --> 00:23:53,265
Hey, sweetie. Come, have a seat.

198
00:23:53,349 --> 00:23:54,350
[Youjin] Okay.

199
00:23:54,433 --> 00:23:56,518
Mom made some refreshing bean sprout soup.

200
00:23:56,602 --> 00:23:58,896
[Youjin] I'm running late,
so I'll have to skip breakfast.

201
00:23:58,979 --> 00:24:00,189
[Miyoung] Come on, how long does it take

202
00:24:00,272 --> 00:24:02,399
-to eat breakfast? Hmm?
-[Youjin] Mmm-mmm.

203
00:24:02,483 --> 00:24:04,693
What's the point of working
if you don't eat?

204
00:24:04,777 --> 00:24:07,029
You're practically skin and bones.

205
00:24:07,613 --> 00:24:09,448
Yeah, have some breakfast before you go.

206
00:24:09,531 --> 00:24:11,450
We'll ask Youseong to give you a ride.

207
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:13,285
Yeah, that would work.

208
00:24:13,369 --> 00:24:16,413
Youseong's giving you a ride today.
Eat before you go.

209
00:24:16,497 --> 00:24:18,165
-I am?
-[Miyoung] Yeah.

210
00:24:18,248 --> 00:24:21,752
Or how about I take Dad's car?
I can drive.

211
00:24:21,835 --> 00:24:23,003
Come on, no.

212
00:24:23,087 --> 00:24:25,255
You still need more practice.

213
00:24:25,339 --> 00:24:27,091
Youseong can give you a ride.

214
00:24:27,174 --> 00:24:28,175
[Miyoung] Yeah, just do that.

215
00:24:28,258 --> 00:24:30,094
-Don't worry. Just sit down and eat.
-[Miyoung] Yeah.

216
00:24:32,721 --> 00:24:34,139
[Miyoung] Come on, let's eat.

217
00:24:36,141 --> 00:24:37,142
Let's eat.

218
00:24:37,226 --> 00:24:38,227
Come on.

219
00:24:38,310 --> 00:24:40,312
-I'll give you a ride.
-[Miyoung] Good. Sit here.

220
00:24:41,146 --> 00:24:42,147
Oh, man.

221
00:25:14,555 --> 00:25:16,140
-Thanks. [in English] Thank you.
-[seatbelt unlocks]

222
00:25:16,223 --> 00:25:17,725
[in Korean] Hey.

223
00:25:17,808 --> 00:25:19,309
Are you going to keep that in?

224
00:25:19,393 --> 00:25:20,394
[Youjin] Oh...

225
00:25:25,441 --> 00:25:26,483
Bye now.

226
00:25:26,567 --> 00:25:27,568
Youjin.

227
00:25:28,318 --> 00:25:29,528
You see,

228
00:25:30,279 --> 00:25:33,949
you're my one and only little sister,

229
00:25:34,700 --> 00:25:38,746
and I really, truly care
about you so much.

230
00:25:38,829 --> 00:25:39,830
What?

231
00:25:40,414 --> 00:25:44,710
[smacks lips] I mean,
sometimes I get in your business,

232
00:25:44,793 --> 00:25:50,466
nag you, or even get pretty scary
and yell at you, right?

233
00:25:52,009 --> 00:25:56,597
But it's all because
I care about you, Youjin. Okay?

234
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:58,474
I just want what's best for you.

235
00:25:59,641 --> 00:26:03,103
I hope you understand
where your big brother is coming from.

236
00:26:04,063 --> 00:26:05,147
It's not scary.

237
00:26:06,148 --> 00:26:07,149
[Youseong] What?

238
00:26:07,941 --> 00:26:09,193
It's not scary.

239
00:26:09,818 --> 00:26:10,903
It's annoying.

240
00:26:14,323 --> 00:26:15,324
Fine.

241
00:26:15,824 --> 00:26:17,117
Get out. Go.

242
00:26:26,335 --> 00:26:27,336
[mumbles] What the hell?

243
00:26:49,483 --> 00:26:50,984
CALLING
+1 617-555-0754

244
00:26:59,910 --> 00:27:02,079
[automation in English] <i>The person</i>
<i>you are calling is not answering...</i>

245
00:27:03,122 --> 00:27:05,082
-[line disconnects]
-[sighs]

246
00:27:05,165 --> 00:27:09,294
Once that brat finds out,
she's going to freak out totally.

247
00:27:24,977 --> 00:27:26,478
Hey, Subin.

248
00:27:26,562 --> 00:27:28,105
Yeah, it's me, Youseong.

249
00:27:30,107 --> 00:27:32,484
Well, I happened to be
at your campus right now.

250
00:27:32,568 --> 00:27:33,694
Do you have a minute?

251
00:27:36,029 --> 00:27:38,699
There's something
I wanted to ask you about Youjin.

252
00:27:39,199 --> 00:27:40,242
Yeah.

253
00:27:40,325 --> 00:27:42,703
No, don't tell Youjin about this.

254
00:27:43,954 --> 00:27:45,122
Yeah.

255
00:27:45,205 --> 00:27:46,415
Okay, got it.

256
00:27:48,125 --> 00:27:50,127
-[mouse clicking]

257
00:27:55,007 --> 00:27:57,259
-[door opens]

258
00:27:58,594 --> 00:28:01,555
[Taeho sighing] All right.
Good morning, everyone.

259
00:28:01,638 --> 00:28:02,973
Good morning.

260
00:28:03,056 --> 00:28:04,224
[Taeho] Mmm-hmm.

261
00:28:11,982 --> 00:28:12,983
All right.

262
00:28:21,992 --> 00:28:23,285
Let's start the meeting.

263
00:28:27,205 --> 00:28:30,375
Finals are over,
so things have settled down.

264
00:28:31,293 --> 00:28:34,379
We've got a lab meeting next week, right?
Whose turn is it?

265
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:36,798
[hesitates] My turn.

266
00:28:37,925 --> 00:28:38,967
Are you ready?

267
00:28:39,051 --> 00:28:41,136
Yeah, well...

268
00:28:42,304 --> 00:28:44,473
The other labs will be there, too.

269
00:28:44,556 --> 00:28:46,016
Our reputation is on the line.

270
00:28:46,683 --> 00:28:49,436
So you'd better be prepared.
Don't embarrass us.

271
00:28:50,312 --> 00:28:51,313
[softly] Okay.

272
00:28:51,396 --> 00:28:53,941
[Hangyeol] But it seemed like
it was getting pushed back a week.

273
00:28:54,024 --> 00:28:55,025
[Taeho] Why?

274
00:28:55,108 --> 00:28:59,363
[Sejin] The Thomas and Dalmatian labs
wanted to reschedule,

275
00:28:59,446 --> 00:29:01,490
since Christmas is next week and all.

276
00:29:01,573 --> 00:29:02,574
[Taeho] Really?

277
00:29:04,034 --> 00:29:06,536
[Sejin sighing] Apparently,
the Thomas guys are going

278
00:29:06,620 --> 00:29:08,872
on a group blind date
with the piano majors.

279
00:29:10,248 --> 00:29:13,627
I think there's almost 100% chance
that they'll reschedule.

280
00:29:13,710 --> 00:29:15,963
-[Taeho sighs heavily]
-Jeez, those crazy bastards...

281
00:29:16,046 --> 00:29:19,591
[chuckling] Wow, sounds like things
are just as messed up over there.

282
00:29:22,219 --> 00:29:26,723
What's with the obsession
with these blind dates? [laughs]

283
00:29:26,807 --> 00:29:29,226
And yet, Korea has the lowest birth rate
in the world.

284
00:29:29,309 --> 00:29:30,894
-Exactly.
-[Taeho] Right?

285
00:29:30,978 --> 00:29:32,938
It's not like we don't want to go on them.

286
00:29:34,731 --> 00:29:38,110
Those damn punks
don't know Christmas is for families.

287
00:29:38,860 --> 00:29:39,861
You'll see.

288
00:29:40,696 --> 00:29:45,617
There's going to be a bloodbath
next semester.

289
00:29:46,451 --> 00:29:47,452
[Chansoo] Hmm.

290
00:29:48,662 --> 00:29:52,457
I guess we can come back
to the lab meeting date next time, then.

291
00:29:53,458 --> 00:29:55,544
Youjin, have you decided
on your thesis topic?

292
00:29:56,753 --> 00:29:59,798
No. I mean, I'm still thinking.

293
00:30:00,424 --> 00:30:03,385
I'm debating between optimal design
and control algorithms,

294
00:30:03,468 --> 00:30:05,971
-but I haven't decided yet.
-[knocks on table]

295
00:30:06,054 --> 00:30:08,724
[Taeho] You've got to hurry, okay?

296
00:30:08,807 --> 00:30:11,143
What's taking you so long, Youjin?

297
00:30:11,768 --> 00:30:12,769
Okay.

298
00:30:14,021 --> 00:30:15,522
[sighs] And you, Sejin?

299
00:30:15,605 --> 00:30:17,649
Yes, I've decided.

300
00:30:18,942 --> 00:30:21,236
You did? What did you pick?

301
00:30:22,696 --> 00:30:24,823
I'm not going to tell you.

302
00:31:51,284 --> 00:31:52,285
[Jihoon] Hey.

303
00:31:56,498 --> 00:32:00,127
If you manage to prove this,
you have to put my name in the paper.

304
00:32:03,505 --> 00:32:05,048
Will you not?

305
00:32:05,132 --> 00:32:06,258
I will.

306
00:32:07,259 --> 00:32:08,885
[Youjin] And give me the prize money, too?

307
00:32:08,969 --> 00:32:11,429
Not all of it, just some. A little bit?

308
00:32:12,180 --> 00:32:15,851
Why are you so obsessed with money?
It's the honor that matters.

309
00:32:16,434 --> 00:32:17,435
So you won't?

310
00:32:18,061 --> 00:32:20,438
There's no prize money.
It's just for the honor.

311
00:32:21,022 --> 00:32:22,023
[Youjin] Hmm.

312
00:32:22,107 --> 00:32:23,942
There's no prize money for this one.

313
00:32:27,404 --> 00:32:30,824
[Jihoon] But I did bring you
something back from the seminar.

314
00:32:30,907 --> 00:32:32,284
It's not chocolate, though.

315
00:32:32,993 --> 00:32:34,161
It's kind of expensive.

316
00:32:35,328 --> 00:32:37,122
You really got me a gift?

317
00:32:37,205 --> 00:32:38,540
Got any plans next Friday?

318
00:32:39,040 --> 00:32:41,168
I'll take you to dinner
and give you your gift.

319
00:32:41,751 --> 00:32:43,545
Okay. Friday works for me, too.

320
00:32:44,504 --> 00:32:46,006
[muttering] 23, 25...

321
00:32:46,756 --> 00:32:49,342
[exclaims] Isn't it Christmas that day?

322
00:32:50,719 --> 00:32:52,053
Is it?

323
00:32:53,638 --> 00:32:56,266
Forget it.
Traffic will be terrible, it'll be packed.

324
00:32:56,349 --> 00:32:57,601
No, it's too troublesome.

325
00:33:02,230 --> 00:33:04,065
[Jihoon] But I don't have time
on any other day.

326
00:33:07,110 --> 00:33:08,403
What do we do?

327
00:33:08,486 --> 00:33:11,114
Then, can we just do Friday?

328
00:33:12,032 --> 00:33:15,660
Places like Gangnam, Hongdae,
and Seongsu will be packed,

329
00:33:15,744 --> 00:33:18,205
but I think it'll be okay around campus.

330
00:33:18,288 --> 00:33:19,414
You think?

331
00:33:19,497 --> 00:33:20,498
[Youjin] Yeah.

332
00:33:22,626 --> 00:33:23,627
Well, then...

333
00:33:24,628 --> 00:33:25,629
I guess why not?

334
00:33:29,633 --> 00:33:32,761
Is there anything you want for Christmas?

335
00:33:32,844 --> 00:33:34,137
There isn't.

336
00:33:34,221 --> 00:33:36,681
Come on, tell me.
This is a rare opportunity.

337
00:33:37,390 --> 00:33:38,975
Just tell me what you want.

338
00:33:44,522 --> 00:33:45,523
Then, you.

339
00:33:52,197 --> 00:33:54,699
I mean, just having a meal with you
is enough.

340
00:33:54,783 --> 00:33:56,576
I don't need any gifts.

341
00:33:57,118 --> 00:33:58,119
[Youjin] Hmm.

342
00:33:58,578 --> 00:34:00,497
So I really don't have
to get you anything?

343
00:34:01,206 --> 00:34:02,582
Because I really won't.

344
00:34:04,376 --> 00:34:06,795
Knowing your taste,
it will end up in the trash anyway.

345
00:34:07,462 --> 00:34:08,964
It's environmental pollution.

346
00:34:09,047 --> 00:34:11,341
We have to pay
to throw stuff away in this country.

347
00:34:14,010 --> 00:34:17,973
[sighs] I bet you wouldn't say that to me
if we were in the US.

348
00:34:20,392 --> 00:34:21,393
What?

349
00:34:21,476 --> 00:34:23,687
I heard they sell guns
at supermarkets in the US.

350
00:34:26,273 --> 00:34:29,276
I hope my gift is a gun.

351
00:34:29,359 --> 00:34:30,360
[Jihoon] Okay.

352
00:34:31,987 --> 00:34:32,988
It's not a gun.

353
00:34:36,324 --> 00:34:37,325
Now, go.

354
00:34:44,416 --> 00:34:48,211
PROFESSOR LEE JIHOON'S OFFICE

355
00:34:48,878 --> 00:34:49,879
[mumbles] I swear to God...

356
00:34:56,219 --> 00:34:57,554
What did I come here for?

357
00:35:11,067 --> 00:35:13,820
I'm going to the library for a bit...

358
00:35:34,883 --> 00:35:36,593
My goodness.

359
00:35:37,260 --> 00:35:39,262
Things are pretty messed up around here.

360
00:35:40,013 --> 00:35:42,307
[Taeho] Seriously,
those assholes have lost their minds

361
00:35:42,390 --> 00:35:46,102
and are pushing back the lab meeting
for some stupid group blind date.

362
00:35:46,186 --> 00:35:50,732
Those damn robot train nerds think
our bipedal humanoid is a fucking joke.

363
00:35:51,524 --> 00:35:55,153
That's why you've got to get back here
and clean house.

364
00:35:55,236 --> 00:35:57,656
We need a full-on bloodbath, Minjae.

365
00:35:58,239 --> 00:36:02,452
[Minjae laughing] What do you mean,
a bloodbath? Don't be crazy.

366
00:36:03,953 --> 00:36:06,539
Hey, so, what about the Dalmatian guys?

367
00:36:08,958 --> 00:36:09,959
Yeah.

368
00:36:10,835 --> 00:36:11,836
Oh, really?

369
00:36:12,879 --> 00:36:14,798
Well, that's the right thing to do.

370
00:36:15,799 --> 00:36:20,428
Those guys are actually really generous.

371
00:36:20,512 --> 00:36:21,638
[Taeho] <i>Come on, Minjae.</i>

372
00:36:21,721 --> 00:36:25,225
<i>This isn't something</i>
<i>you can just laugh off, okay?</i>

373
00:36:25,809 --> 00:36:28,311
I'm telling you,
you need to get back here, Minjae.

374
00:36:28,395 --> 00:36:30,063
When are you coming back, anyway?

375
00:36:30,855 --> 00:36:32,857
Yeah, but when? Hmm?

376
00:36:32,941 --> 00:36:34,234
Mmm.

377
00:36:34,317 --> 00:36:36,653
Really? [chuckles]

378
00:36:36,736 --> 00:36:38,571
Yeah, of course. I'll keep it to myself.

379
00:36:38,655 --> 00:36:40,448
None of the other guys will know. Yeah.

380
00:36:41,032 --> 00:36:44,035
Got it. But, Minjae,
you really have to be here that day, okay?

381
00:36:44,119 --> 00:36:45,954
Okay, enough already.

382
00:36:47,247 --> 00:36:49,791
Just stop.
[chuckling] I said I got it, you weirdo.

383
00:36:51,251 --> 00:36:52,377
All right.

384
00:36:52,460 --> 00:36:55,755
I'll call you back. Bye.

385
00:37:05,849 --> 00:37:08,268
Mom, just leave it.
I can take care of it later.

386
00:37:08,351 --> 00:37:09,644
[Eunjoo] It's okay. I'm done.

387
00:37:09,728 --> 00:37:11,521
[Minjae] No, let me... Gosh.

388
00:37:11,604 --> 00:37:14,524
-You want this up there?
-[Eunjoo] Yeah. [laughs]

389
00:37:14,607 --> 00:37:18,987
Goodness. It's so nice
having someone tall around.

390
00:37:19,070 --> 00:37:20,947
[Minjae] Now, leave it.
I'll deal with them later.

391
00:37:21,030 --> 00:37:22,073
-[Eunjoo] Okay.
-[Minjae] Come on.

392
00:37:22,657 --> 00:37:24,701
-Can I have a glass of water?
-[Minjae] Sure.

393
00:37:38,840 --> 00:37:42,010
My glasses... Where did I put the glasses?

394
00:37:42,093 --> 00:37:44,179
Don't bother.
I can just drink it like that.

395
00:37:44,262 --> 00:37:45,472
-Yeah?
-[Eunjoo] Yeah.

396
00:37:48,349 --> 00:37:50,894
-I should get a new glass.
-[Eunjoo chuckles]

397
00:37:52,020 --> 00:37:53,021
Yeah.

398
00:37:54,856 --> 00:37:56,983
[Eunjoo] There were so many
little things to unpack.

399
00:37:57,066 --> 00:37:58,526
And so much dust.

400
00:37:59,402 --> 00:38:02,405
If I'd known it would be this much work,
I would've hired someone.

401
00:38:02,489 --> 00:38:04,073
[Minjae] No, it's okay. Later...

402
00:38:04,157 --> 00:38:06,618
I'll take my time
unpacking everything later.

403
00:38:11,664 --> 00:38:15,293
[Eunjoo] You didn't forget
what you promised me, right?

404
00:38:18,046 --> 00:38:19,380
No drinking.

405
00:38:20,715 --> 00:38:23,760
No wine or beer, nothing.

406
00:38:25,345 --> 00:38:26,346
[mumbles] Fine.

407
00:38:26,429 --> 00:38:29,307
And make sure
to get at least eight hours of sleep.

408
00:38:29,390 --> 00:38:32,060
Eat balanced meals.

409
00:38:32,143 --> 00:38:34,187
Don't skip your workouts.

410
00:38:34,270 --> 00:38:36,272
I'm going to be checking.

411
00:38:36,356 --> 00:38:38,024
[chuckling] What...
What do you mean, checking?

412
00:38:38,107 --> 00:38:40,068
I'm not a kid. I can take care of myself.

413
00:38:40,151 --> 00:38:43,863
You saw how your grandfather and aunt
were freaking out,

414
00:38:43,947 --> 00:38:46,324
saying I was trying
to sneak you back to Korea,

415
00:38:46,825 --> 00:38:47,992
Right?

416
00:38:48,076 --> 00:38:49,994
I've gotten more grief
in the past few days

417
00:38:50,078 --> 00:38:51,579
than I have in my entire life.

418
00:38:56,042 --> 00:38:58,336
You owe me for this, okay?

419
00:38:58,419 --> 00:38:59,712
So keep your promise.

420
00:39:00,505 --> 00:39:01,756
Fine, I will.

421
00:39:01,840 --> 00:39:02,882
[Eunjoo] All right.

422
00:39:03,466 --> 00:39:05,385
I should get going now.

423
00:39:05,468 --> 00:39:06,469
Okay.

424
00:39:06,553 --> 00:39:07,846
I'll be back tomorrow.

425
00:39:08,513 --> 00:39:10,265
You don't have to. I know you're busy.

426
00:39:10,348 --> 00:39:12,350
You should get going.
Your husband is waiting.

427
00:39:12,433 --> 00:39:16,271
He's never home before midnight.
He's not waiting. [chuckles softly]

428
00:39:16,354 --> 00:39:18,106
[Minjae] Well, Juwon is waiting.
Come on, go.

429
00:39:18,189 --> 00:39:20,525
[Eunjoo] Gosh,
when will he get into college?

430
00:39:23,820 --> 00:39:25,405
[Eunjoo] No, you don't need to come out.

431
00:39:25,488 --> 00:39:27,574
[Minjae] Let me at least walk you
to the elevator.

432
00:39:36,457 --> 00:39:39,168
I'm going to send someone over tomorrow,
so just leave everything.

433
00:39:39,252 --> 00:39:40,837
-[elevator dings]
-[Minjae] No need to send anyone.

434
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:43,590
-It's fine. I can take care of it.
-[elevator dings]

435
00:39:43,673 --> 00:39:48,094
Keep disobeying Mom, and you'll have
to go back to Canada. Okay?

436
00:39:48,177 --> 00:39:49,554
All right. Fine, I get it.

437
00:39:50,680 --> 00:39:51,806
Get back inside.

438
00:39:51,890 --> 00:39:53,892
Let me wait till the elevator gets here.

439
00:39:54,809 --> 00:39:56,352
I'll be fine. Get back inside.

440
00:39:58,187 --> 00:39:59,188
-[elevator dings]
-[Eunjoo] There.

441
00:39:59,272 --> 00:40:00,481
-I'm going to go.
-[Minjae] Okay.

442
00:40:02,108 --> 00:40:03,610
-Bye.
-[Eunjoo] Bye.

443
00:40:04,652 --> 00:40:06,738
[automation] <i>Doors closing. First floor.</i>

444
00:40:06,821 --> 00:40:07,822
Bye.

445
00:40:57,789 --> 00:41:00,875
Hello. Please scan your student ID.

446
00:41:00,959 --> 00:41:01,960
Okay.

447
00:41:07,006 --> 00:41:08,883
-Is all of your information correct?
-Yes.

448
00:41:21,980 --> 00:41:23,398
Please return it in a week.

449
00:41:23,481 --> 00:41:24,565
Thank you.

450
00:41:34,659 --> 00:41:35,660
[loudly] Subin!

451
00:41:54,303 --> 00:41:55,847
So, what did you say?

452
00:41:57,181 --> 00:41:59,308
[Youseong] I don't remember what I said.

453
00:41:59,392 --> 00:42:03,187
I've been drinking a lot lately,
so my memory hasn't been that great.

454
00:42:05,481 --> 00:42:09,318
I just remember a lot of crying
and drama on the phone.

455
00:42:09,902 --> 00:42:12,655
[Subin] He did? He cried on the phone?

456
00:42:12,739 --> 00:42:14,073
No, me.

457
00:42:14,157 --> 00:42:15,158
What?

458
00:42:16,034 --> 00:42:17,160
But why would you?

459
00:42:18,870 --> 00:42:21,289
Well, I don't really remember,

460
00:42:21,372 --> 00:42:23,124
but I had my reasons for crying.

461
00:42:23,207 --> 00:42:24,917
I cried my eyes out.

462
00:42:25,918 --> 00:42:27,628
Anyway, the point is that,

463
00:42:27,712 --> 00:42:31,632
that jerk said he only broke up
with Youjin because I told him to.

464
00:42:31,716 --> 00:42:33,468
He was using me as an excuse.

465
00:42:33,551 --> 00:42:34,802
Oh...

466
00:42:34,886 --> 00:42:38,014
Did you tell Minjae
to break up with Youjin?

467
00:42:38,097 --> 00:42:39,098
Well...

468
00:42:40,349 --> 00:42:44,062
All I said was that, as her brother,
I didn't think someone like him

469
00:42:44,145 --> 00:42:47,565
was a good fit for my little sister.
That's what I said.

470
00:42:47,648 --> 00:42:50,443
But it's not really about
whether they're a good fit.

471
00:42:50,526 --> 00:42:53,112
If they like each other,
there's nothing you can do.

472
00:42:53,196 --> 00:42:56,449
[sighs] Youjin is gonna freak out
if she finds out.

473
00:42:56,532 --> 00:42:58,159
She's terrifying when she's angry.

474
00:42:58,743 --> 00:43:00,787
Like that little brat can scare me.

475
00:43:03,206 --> 00:43:06,084
Subin, don't tell Youjin about this, okay?

476
00:43:09,128 --> 00:43:11,380
Seriously, you can't
tell anyone about this.

477
00:43:14,008 --> 00:43:15,426
Fine.

478
00:43:18,137 --> 00:43:22,183
Anyway, he's been holding this huge grudge
against me all this time,

479
00:43:22,266 --> 00:43:23,851
and now he's coming back to Korea.

480
00:43:29,107 --> 00:43:31,692
Wait, he's coming back to Korea? When?

481
00:43:32,401 --> 00:43:33,611
[Youseong] Pretty soon, apparently.

482
00:43:36,489 --> 00:43:40,368
So, Subin,
if that jerk shows up around Youjin,

483
00:43:40,451 --> 00:43:42,203
make sure they don't meet.

484
00:43:42,286 --> 00:43:43,746
What? Me?

485
00:43:44,539 --> 00:43:47,750
[Youseong] Yeah, don't let them meet.
Don't let him anywhere near her.

486
00:43:48,292 --> 00:43:50,294
How can I do that?

487
00:43:50,378 --> 00:43:52,922
Well, you'll have
to figure that out yourself.

488
00:43:53,005 --> 00:43:55,591
I don't think there's any way
to keep them from meeting.

489
00:43:57,844 --> 00:43:58,845
There's no way.

490
00:43:59,637 --> 00:44:01,013
[Youseong] Of course, there is.

491
00:44:01,097 --> 00:44:04,225
Use that big Seohan brain of yours
and think of something.

492
00:44:04,308 --> 00:44:06,894
There's no way to do that.

493
00:44:14,527 --> 00:44:15,528
Then...

494
00:44:16,904 --> 00:44:18,489
you stay right by her side.

495
00:44:18,573 --> 00:44:19,574
What?

496
00:44:20,366 --> 00:44:22,577
Then, once that jerk shows up
in front of Youjin,

497
00:44:22,660 --> 00:44:25,163
call me right away. I'll come running.

498
00:44:27,498 --> 00:44:30,626
[Subin] Maybe it's okay to let them meet.

499
00:44:31,544 --> 00:44:32,712
[Youseong] Why?

500
00:44:32,795 --> 00:44:35,673
Youjin is never going
to forgive Minjae, anyway.

501
00:44:37,175 --> 00:44:39,218
She liked him so much.

502
00:44:40,803 --> 00:44:44,140
But he just dumped her out of nowhere,
without even giving her a reason.

503
00:44:44,849 --> 00:44:47,143
You have no idea how hard that was on her.

504
00:44:47,226 --> 00:44:50,646
After all that, there's no way
she'd get back together with him.

505
00:44:52,648 --> 00:44:55,943
Besides, you know how stubborn Youjin is.

506
00:44:56,527 --> 00:44:57,987
-She'd never want to meet him.
-[Youseong sighs]

507
00:44:58,070 --> 00:45:01,157
I mean, they broke up because of me.

508
00:45:03,451 --> 00:45:05,036
[Subin] So, what if you didn't approve?

509
00:45:05,119 --> 00:45:07,663
He broke up with her just because of that?

510
00:45:07,747 --> 00:45:09,290
That's actually even worse.

511
00:45:10,708 --> 00:45:12,960
Well, I think it's possible.

512
00:45:13,044 --> 00:45:15,671
But I'm more worried about him
messing with her head again

513
00:45:15,755 --> 00:45:18,132
than about them getting back together.

514
00:45:18,216 --> 00:45:20,051
Youjin is seeing someone now,

515
00:45:20,134 --> 00:45:22,053
and it could cause misunderstandings, too.

516
00:45:22,136 --> 00:45:23,137
Oh...

517
00:45:23,888 --> 00:45:26,766
Is Youjin seeing someone?

518
00:45:33,231 --> 00:45:35,066
[Jaehong] Starting next semester,

519
00:45:35,775 --> 00:45:38,444
I'm thinking of splitting a few areas
into smaller teams

520
00:45:38,527 --> 00:45:39,904
and reorganizing things a bit.

521
00:45:40,529 --> 00:45:41,530
[Jihoon] I see.

522
00:45:42,323 --> 00:45:44,992
[Jaehong] I'm also thinking...

523
00:45:45,076 --> 00:45:46,744
...of developing a diffusion model,

524
00:45:47,411 --> 00:45:50,081
and I thought it might be nice
to have you join us

525
00:45:50,915 --> 00:45:53,459
for a collaborative research project.

526
00:45:53,542 --> 00:45:56,003
That's why I invited you here today.

527
00:45:56,587 --> 00:45:59,507
I've got a lot on my plate these days,
so I don't think I can.

528
00:46:00,049 --> 00:46:02,426
Come on, join us.
It's a win-win for both of us.

529
00:46:02,510 --> 00:46:04,512
Seriously. I can't, even if I wanted to.

530
00:46:06,847 --> 00:46:09,058
I could send some of my students
to help out.

531
00:46:09,934 --> 00:46:13,312
No, we need to work with our own students
to help them grow.

532
00:46:13,396 --> 00:46:15,648
I was thinking
of getting Lim Youjin involved.

533
00:46:17,650 --> 00:46:18,776
Lim Youjin.

534
00:46:20,152 --> 00:46:23,406
Lim Youjin could be a good choice.
That should work.

535
00:46:24,240 --> 00:46:25,866
See, with diffusion models,

536
00:46:25,950 --> 00:46:29,370
even a single equation can involve
some pretty complicated math.

537
00:46:29,453 --> 00:46:33,457
She may not be the most efficient worker,

538
00:46:33,541 --> 00:46:37,253
but she's stubborn as hell,
so I think she'll do a good job.

539
00:46:37,336 --> 00:46:39,171
I've noticed this for a while now.

540
00:46:40,464 --> 00:46:44,552
One minute,
you've got these dead, lifeless eyes,

541
00:46:44,635 --> 00:46:46,429
and the second Youjin is mentioned,

542
00:46:46,512 --> 00:46:49,181
your eyes light right up.

543
00:46:50,266 --> 00:46:51,267
What?

544
00:46:51,350 --> 00:46:55,104
I mean, who knows
where you'll find the one, right?

545
00:46:57,315 --> 00:46:59,483
What do you mean by "the one"?

546
00:47:00,067 --> 00:47:02,320
Well, love works
in mysterious ways, you know.

547
00:47:04,822 --> 00:47:06,699
Jeez, what's with Koreans

548
00:47:06,782 --> 00:47:08,826
and their obsession
with dating and marriage?

549
00:47:09,744 --> 00:47:10,995
[Jaehong] What?

550
00:47:11,078 --> 00:47:13,831
That is a kid
you're supposed to be supervising.

551
00:47:15,124 --> 00:47:16,584
Wait, what... I was just...

552
00:47:16,667 --> 00:47:18,794
You can't say things like that these days.

553
00:47:23,466 --> 00:47:25,676
I don't think what I said
was that inappropriate.

554
00:47:25,760 --> 00:47:28,554
But what's this about?
Did I do something to upset you?

555
00:47:28,637 --> 00:47:30,431
No, you didn't.

556
00:47:31,724 --> 00:47:33,934
She's young
and has years of study ahead of her.

557
00:47:34,018 --> 00:47:36,812
It wouldn't do her any good
if people spread rumors about her.

558
00:47:38,856 --> 00:47:42,026
You know that.
Remember when I first got hired here?

559
00:47:42,109 --> 00:47:43,986
Everyone talked about me being too young,

560
00:47:44,070 --> 00:47:46,280
lacking the right background,
and my personality...

561
00:47:46,364 --> 00:47:47,698
There was so much gossip.

562
00:47:48,657 --> 00:47:50,868
Even now, thinking about it
keeps me up at night.

563
00:47:50,951 --> 00:47:52,453
That's how bad it was.

564
00:47:54,580 --> 00:47:57,458
You know better than anyone
how much I went through.

565
00:47:59,710 --> 00:48:01,629
You bought me more drinks
than anyone else.

566
00:48:02,421 --> 00:48:03,881
Knowing all that, how could you...

567
00:48:06,759 --> 00:48:10,304
[chuckling] Right, drinks...
I did buy you quite a few drinks.

568
00:48:11,514 --> 00:48:13,933
I've got some papers
on the diffusion model.

569
00:48:14,016 --> 00:48:15,684
-I'll send them over.
-Okay, sure.

570
00:48:18,437 --> 00:48:21,440
So there's going to be
a major restructuring next semester?

571
00:48:21,524 --> 00:48:24,360
I'm thinking of breaking it down
into more specialized teams

572
00:48:24,443 --> 00:48:26,112
to strengthen our expertise.

573
00:48:27,029 --> 00:48:30,408
And Park Minjae is joining us
next semester, too.

574
00:48:31,784 --> 00:48:33,911
I heard that you two met up in the States?

575
00:48:35,037 --> 00:48:36,038
Yeah.

576
00:48:36,122 --> 00:48:37,456
Is he coming back to Korea?

577
00:48:37,540 --> 00:48:38,582
Yes.

578
00:48:38,666 --> 00:48:42,461
I begged him
on my hands and knees to return,

579
00:48:42,545 --> 00:48:44,672
and it must've moved him.
He's coming back.

580
00:48:45,798 --> 00:48:46,799
I see. That's great.

581
00:48:47,758 --> 00:48:50,428
He'll lead one of the teams
and teach a course.

582
00:48:52,054 --> 00:48:53,055
Okay.

583
00:48:55,766 --> 00:48:58,602
-[Taeho] Wait, but how did you know?
-I just heard it.

584
00:48:58,686 --> 00:49:01,647
Yeah, I mean,
I haven't told anyone about it.

585
00:49:01,730 --> 00:49:03,315
Where did you hear that?

586
00:49:03,399 --> 00:49:05,359
He's got a superpower. Like Sommers.

587
00:49:05,443 --> 00:49:07,278
-[Hangyeol scoffs]
-Dude, kids these days

588
00:49:07,361 --> 00:49:08,779
don't know who Sommers is.

589
00:49:08,863 --> 00:49:09,989
[Sejin] I know Sommers.

590
00:49:10,072 --> 00:49:13,534
You know Sommers? Good for you, nerd.

591
00:49:15,286 --> 00:49:19,457
Jeez, it was going to be a surprise,
and Sommers ruined everything.

592
00:49:19,540 --> 00:49:21,083
-[Chansoo] So...
-[Hangyeol] Huh?

593
00:49:21,167 --> 00:49:24,003
What? What is it? What surprise?

594
00:49:24,086 --> 00:49:27,298
Minjae's finished with his postdoc
and is coming back to Korea.

595
00:50:13,552 --> 00:50:15,387
-[cashier] Please insert your card.
-[Minjae] All right.

596
00:50:15,471 --> 00:50:17,806
"Jingle Bells"]

597
00:50:24,522 --> 00:50:26,023
-[cashier] Do you need a receipt?
-[Minjae] I'm good.

598
00:50:28,400 --> 00:50:30,402
-[bell jingles]

599
00:50:51,048 --> 00:50:52,800
-[church bell tolling]

600
00:51:06,647 --> 00:51:08,315
Persistent much?

601
00:51:09,817 --> 00:51:12,528
I'm not going to buy it.
I'm not buying it.

602
00:53:21,073 --> 00:53:23,075
Gigliola Cinquetti "Non Ho L'Età"]

603
00:54:35,981 --> 00:54:36,982
[softly] Who is it?

604
00:54:39,818 --> 00:54:40,819
Hello?

605
00:54:43,822 --> 00:54:44,823
Hello?

606
00:54:47,659 --> 00:54:48,660
Hello?

607
00:54:51,705 --> 00:54:52,706
Hel...

608
00:54:54,833 --> 00:54:57,628
Mr. Lim Youseong.
Are you drunk-dialing me again?

609
00:55:00,464 --> 00:55:02,341
Yes, Professor.

610
00:55:02,424 --> 00:55:03,926
Yes, this is Park Minjae.

611
00:55:04,009 --> 00:55:05,385
No, it's me.

612
00:55:06,386 --> 00:55:08,639
I thought it was someone else.

613
00:55:10,307 --> 00:55:11,308
Tomorrow?

614
00:55:12,726 --> 00:55:14,311
Right, yes. I know where it is.

615
00:55:15,062 --> 00:55:17,523
Yes. At 7:00...

616
00:55:17,606 --> 00:55:19,024
Yeah, 7:00 works for me.

617
00:55:19,775 --> 00:55:22,528
Yes. Okay, see you then.

618
00:55:23,195 --> 00:55:24,196
Bye.

619
00:55:30,869 --> 00:55:31,870
[mumbles] What...

620
00:55:36,917 --> 00:55:38,001
[staff] Hello.

621
00:55:38,085 --> 00:55:39,086
[Minjae] Hello.

622
00:55:39,753 --> 00:55:40,754
[staff] How many people?

623
00:55:41,296 --> 00:55:42,297
Two.

624
00:55:42,381 --> 00:55:43,715
All right. Right this way.

625
00:55:46,134 --> 00:55:47,261
[mumbles] Thank you.

626
00:55:49,846 --> 00:55:51,557
[staff] Let me know whenever you're ready.

627
00:55:51,640 --> 00:55:53,392
[Minjae] All right. Thank you.

628
00:56:05,153 --> 00:56:06,905
-[staff] Hello.
-[Youjin] Hello.

629
00:56:10,200 --> 00:56:11,577
[staff] Let me show you to your table.

630
00:57:06,506 --> 00:57:07,841
-[staff] Hello.
-Hello.

631
00:57:07,924 --> 00:57:09,259
-[Minjae] Hello.
-Hey.

632
00:57:09,926 --> 00:57:12,179
-You're sitting separately? Come here.
-[Minjae] Sorry?

633
00:57:12,804 --> 00:57:13,805
[Jihoon] Come here.

634
00:57:18,310 --> 00:57:19,436
Yeah. Come sit here.

635
00:57:20,020 --> 00:57:21,438
You too, come over.

636
00:57:26,068 --> 00:57:29,529
Sorry, I'm late. Traffic was insane.
The roads were absolutely packed.

637
00:57:30,238 --> 00:57:31,448
-Thank you.
-Sure.

638
00:57:32,991 --> 00:57:35,994
Uh, let's order something
before we start talking.

639
00:57:36,078 --> 00:57:39,122
Their sea urchin and fish roe pasta
is really good.

640
00:57:42,334 --> 00:57:44,378
Hold on. I need to take this.

641
00:57:44,461 --> 00:57:46,254
-You guys go ahead and order.
-[Minjae] Okay.

642
00:57:46,338 --> 00:57:47,339
[Jihoon] Yes, hello?

643
00:57:49,383 --> 00:57:50,384
Yeah.

644
00:57:58,225 --> 00:57:59,476
Would you like to order?

645
00:58:00,185 --> 00:58:02,020
[Youjin] Sorry. Excuse me for a second.

646
00:58:03,689 --> 00:58:04,898
We'll order in a minute.

647
00:58:12,739 --> 00:58:13,740
[Jihoon] Yeah, why?

648
00:58:16,201 --> 00:58:17,786
What do you think you're doing?

649
00:58:18,745 --> 00:58:19,955
I'm on the phone.

650
00:58:20,038 --> 00:58:21,123
Yes.

651
00:58:22,624 --> 00:58:25,460
How long will it take?
The sooner, the better for me.

652
00:58:27,713 --> 00:58:28,714
Okay.

653
00:58:29,464 --> 00:58:30,841
Yeah, got it.

654
00:58:32,926 --> 00:58:34,386
Why did you invite him?

655
00:58:35,721 --> 00:58:37,723
[Jihoon] I had to.
He said he'd be alone on Christmas.

656
00:58:37,806 --> 00:58:39,224
Can't we just hang out?

657
00:58:39,307 --> 00:58:41,101
We're not in the US, okay?

658
00:58:41,184 --> 00:58:44,020
Who eats and hangs out with their ex?

659
00:58:44,104 --> 00:58:46,022
It's too late now. Do I tell him to leave?

660
00:58:46,106 --> 00:58:47,649
[Youjin] Yeah, tell him to leave.

661
00:58:59,786 --> 00:59:01,830
-Enjoy.
-All right. Thank you.

662
00:59:20,265 --> 00:59:22,392
How long are you going to be sitting here?

663
00:59:31,234 --> 00:59:33,695
-No, don't.
-Just let me.

664
00:59:41,953 --> 00:59:45,290
You're already letting him win
by acting like this.

665
00:59:45,916 --> 00:59:48,835
Look at Minjae. See how confident he is.
He's totally fine.

666
00:59:50,837 --> 00:59:52,506
You've got to act confident, too.

667
00:59:53,340 --> 00:59:56,843
Like, "I'm fine, too.
I'm doing great without you.

668
00:59:56,927 --> 00:59:59,679
"You're the idiot
who let a woman like me go.'"

669
01:00:01,431 --> 01:00:04,142
Don't run away. Don't hide.
Hold your head high.

670
01:00:05,560 --> 01:00:06,978
I'm not hiding.

671
01:00:07,604 --> 01:00:10,440
It's just awkward and uncomfortable.

672
01:00:10,524 --> 01:00:13,026
Better awkward now than later.

673
01:00:13,109 --> 01:00:15,737
You'll be seeing him at school
next semester, anyway.

674
01:00:16,696 --> 01:00:18,114
He's coming back to our school?

675
01:00:18,782 --> 01:00:20,450
Professor Ahn said he's coming back.

676
01:00:21,117 --> 01:00:23,537
Now, that's just low. He's got no shame.

677
01:00:25,080 --> 01:00:27,582
You need to talk to him face-to-face
at least once.

678
01:00:29,709 --> 01:00:32,003
Then you can finally let go
and start healing.

679
01:00:32,087 --> 01:00:34,422
I have nothing to let go of or heal from.

680
01:00:34,506 --> 01:00:36,591
If you have nothing to let go of
or heal from,

681
01:00:36,675 --> 01:00:38,718
why are we sitting here
in the freezing cold?

682
01:00:44,224 --> 01:00:46,226
You go ahead and go home.

683
01:00:47,352 --> 01:00:48,353
[Jihoon] What?

684
01:00:50,730 --> 01:00:53,817
I'm the one who made this mess.
I should be the one to fix it.

685
01:00:54,651 --> 01:00:56,653
over speakers]

686
01:01:07,080 --> 01:01:08,540
Where's Professor Lee?

687
01:01:10,458 --> 01:01:12,794
Something urgent came up,
so he headed home early.

688
01:01:13,837 --> 01:01:14,838
[Minjae] Oh...

689
01:01:18,008 --> 01:01:20,886
Well, it was taking too long,
so I just ordered whatever.

690
01:01:21,553 --> 01:01:22,554
[Youjin] Hmm.

691
01:01:24,014 --> 01:01:26,474
Okay. Let's eat and get going, too.
Go ahead.

692
01:01:27,183 --> 01:01:29,269
[Minjae mumbling] Yeah, eat up.
Hurry up and eat.

693
01:01:49,414 --> 01:01:51,374
It feels like it's been a while.

694
01:01:53,209 --> 01:01:55,003
When did you come back to Korea?

695
01:01:57,047 --> 01:01:58,882
Just a few days ago.

696
01:02:02,844 --> 01:02:04,596
I hear you'll come back to our school.

697
01:02:04,679 --> 01:02:05,680
Yeah.

698
01:02:06,806 --> 01:02:10,018
Could you maybe consider somewhere else?

699
01:02:11,686 --> 01:02:14,064
No. I'm sorry.

700
01:02:15,982 --> 01:02:17,943
You're always saying that you're sorry.

701
01:02:22,405 --> 01:02:25,742
I heard that you went to Canada
because your grandmother was sick.

702
01:02:25,825 --> 01:02:27,202
Is she doing better now?

703
01:02:30,455 --> 01:02:31,456
[Minjae] Actually,

704
01:02:32,415 --> 01:02:34,501
it wasn't my grandmother who was sick.

705
01:02:35,168 --> 01:02:36,670
I was the one who was a bit sick.

706
01:02:40,590 --> 01:02:41,758
You were sick?

707
01:02:42,676 --> 01:02:43,927
Sick where?

708
01:02:44,636 --> 01:02:46,221
They found a tumor in my lung.

709
01:02:47,514 --> 01:02:50,392
They didn't know
if the osteosarcoma had spread there or...

710
01:02:50,475 --> 01:02:52,227
They weren't sure what caused it,

711
01:02:53,269 --> 01:02:54,771
but there was a tumor.

712
01:02:56,648 --> 01:02:58,984
I'm okay now, though.

713
01:03:00,110 --> 01:03:03,196
The surgery went well,
and I've finished chemo.

714
01:03:04,990 --> 01:03:06,700
Why didn't you tell me?

715
01:03:06,783 --> 01:03:08,660
Because I didn't want to worry you.

716
01:03:08,743 --> 01:03:10,537
Of course, I would've worried.

717
01:03:12,789 --> 01:03:14,708
I know. That's why I didn't tell you.

718
01:03:18,962 --> 01:03:20,463
I had no idea.

719
01:03:20,547 --> 01:03:22,298
Because I didn't tell you.

720
01:03:24,300 --> 01:03:25,802
[Youjin] Why didn't you tell me?

721
01:03:27,095 --> 01:03:29,472
I told you. I didn't want to worry you.

722
01:03:29,556 --> 01:03:32,142
It would've been natural for me to worry.
And maybe...

723
01:03:33,601 --> 01:03:35,311
we didn't even have to break up.

724
01:03:39,107 --> 01:03:41,484
I thought you just got sick
and tired of me.

725
01:03:41,568 --> 01:03:43,486
And that's why you wanted to break up.

726
01:03:45,822 --> 01:03:46,948
[Minjae] Okay.

727
01:03:47,032 --> 01:03:49,075
[sighs] What do you mean by "okay?"

728
01:03:54,748 --> 01:03:57,459
If you kept it a secret
because you didn't want to worry me,

729
01:03:58,126 --> 01:04:00,003
why didn't you keep it that way?

730
01:04:01,212 --> 01:04:02,589
Why are you telling me now?

731
01:04:06,843 --> 01:04:10,180
Did you think I'd forgive you
and take you back? That's ridiculous.

732
01:04:10,263 --> 01:04:11,431
No.

733
01:04:11,514 --> 01:04:14,601
So why tell me now?
You should've just kept it to yourself.

734
01:04:22,233 --> 01:04:24,152
I heard that you were getting married.

735
01:04:27,113 --> 01:04:29,574
Your brother told me
that you're getting married.

736
01:04:31,201 --> 01:04:35,997
My brother said that I'm getting married?

737
01:04:37,791 --> 01:04:39,375
You're making the right choice.

738
01:04:41,503 --> 01:04:44,506
If there's anything on your mind,

739
01:04:45,673 --> 01:04:47,175
let it all out.

740
01:04:58,895 --> 01:04:59,896
Oh...

741
01:05:03,399 --> 01:05:07,779
You wanted to congratulate me
on getting married?

742
01:05:13,368 --> 01:05:14,744
What a big man you are.

743
01:05:17,205 --> 01:05:20,041
I'm really not.
That's why I'm doing this here.

744
01:05:22,210 --> 01:05:23,711
Thank you.

745
01:05:23,795 --> 01:05:26,589
I'll be sure to live happily ever after
with my wonderful man.

746
01:06:10,383 --> 01:06:11,384
You see, I...

747
01:06:13,595 --> 01:06:15,138
What's wrong? Are you okay?

748
01:06:15,722 --> 01:06:19,851
I can't breathe... [groans]

749
01:06:39,162 --> 01:06:40,955
-[Jihoon] Uh...
-Yes.

750
01:06:41,039 --> 01:06:42,040
[Jihoon] Well...

751
01:06:42,916 --> 01:06:46,920
It's just, Youjin left this behind, so...

752
01:06:47,629 --> 01:06:49,130
[Jihoon] Okay. Thanks.

753
01:07:05,230 --> 01:07:07,649
Let's call it a night for now.
We can talk later.

754
01:10:01,781 --> 01:10:05,702
BETWEEN STEPS

755
01:10:41,821 --> 01:10:43,448
[Youjin] <i>He told me to let it all out</i>

756
01:10:43,531 --> 01:10:45,908
<i>and live happily ever after</i>
<i>with my husband.</i>

757
01:10:45,992 --> 01:10:48,745
<i>He invited me to see how I'd react.</i>

758
01:10:48,828 --> 01:10:51,122
<i>She's trying so hard to move on.</i>

759
01:10:51,205 --> 01:10:53,541
<i>Why are you back?</i>
<i>What are you still hung up on?</i>

760
01:10:53,624 --> 01:10:56,085
I'm not back because I haven't moved on.

761
01:10:56,169 --> 01:10:57,336
So just fuck off.

762
01:10:57,920 --> 01:11:00,548
<i>It was better to hurt her a little now</i>

763
01:11:00,631 --> 01:11:02,133
<i>than hurt her even more later. Am I wrong?</i>

764
01:11:03,009 --> 01:11:05,261
<i>I know I messed up, too.</i>

765
01:11:06,554 --> 01:11:08,222
Can we get back together?
